G0467.def:
ἀντ-απο-δίδωμι
(ἀντί ἀποδίδωμι), [in LXX for שָׁלַם pi., גָּמַל, שׁוּב hi., etc. ;] 
to give back as an equivalent, recompense, requital (the ἀντί ex­pressing the idea of full, complete return; see Lft., Notes, 46); 
__(a) in favourable sense: Luc 14:14, Romains 11:35, 1 Thessaloniciens 3:9; 
__(b) in unfavourable sense: Romains 12:19, 2 Thessaloniciens 1:6, Hébreux 10:30.†

G0468.def:
ἀντ-από-δομα, -τος, τό
(ἀνταποδίδωμι) [in LXX chiefly for גְּמוּל ;] ( = cl. -δοσις, which see) 
requital; 
__(a) in favourable sense: Luc 14:12; 
__(b) in unfavourable sense: Romains 11:9.†

G0478.def:
ἀντι-καθ-ίστημι 
[in LXX: Deutéronome 31:21 (עָנָה), Josué 5:7, Michée 2:8 (קוּם) * ;] 
__1. causal in Pres. imperfect fut. and 1 aor.; to replace, oppose. 
__2. Intrans. in pass. and 2 aor. act.; 
__(a) to supersede; 
__(b) to resist: Hébreux 12:4.†

G0482.def:
ἀντι-λαμβάνω 
[frequently in LXX for חָזַק hi., סָמַךְ, etc ;] 
to take instead of or in turn. Mid., with genitive, to take hold of; 
__(a) of persons, to help (see MM, VGT, see word): Luc 1:54, Actes 20:35; 
__(b) of things, to partake of: 1 Timothée 6:2 (see Field, Notes, 210; Cremer, 386; and cf. συν-αντιλαμβάνω).†

G0499.def:
ἀντί-τυπος, -ον
(see: τύπος), [in LXX: Esther 3:13 A * ;] 
__1. active striking back; metaphorically, resisting, adverse. 
__2. Pass. struck back; metaphorically, corres­ponding to (MM, VGT, see word); 
__(a) as impression of a seal or copy of an archetype (τύπος) (RV, Like in pattern), Hébreux 9:24; 
__(b) as the reality (of which τύπος is the copy or adumbration) (RV, after a true likeness), 1 Pierre 3:21 (Cramer, 357).†
